        "cnm_p205"
      ],
      "explanation": "The phrase “\\(x\\%\\) greater than \\(B\\)” measures the increase relative to \\(B\\). The increase from \\(B\\) to \\(A\\) is \\(A-B\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{100}B=A-B.\n\\]\nSince \\(B>0\\), we may divide by \\(B\\), obtaining\n\\[\nx=100\\left(\\frac{A-B}{B}\\right).\n\\]\nThis is choice A.",
